.dev.vars

# Environment variables. .env IS tracked on purpose (see .env.example
# and README): Lovable Cloud's Secrets panel refuses VITE_-prefixed
# keys ("build-time browser values should be defined in .env files,
# not in secrets"), so the Vite/Supabase publishable values that need
# to be baked into the client bundle have to live in a committed .env.
# They're publishable/anon keys, safe to expose to the browser. Real
# secrets (ADMIN_SECRET, WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_URL, the Supabase service
# role key) live in Lovable Cloud's Secrets panel instead, never here.
.env.local
.env.*.local

